opp":"NU","oppName":"Northwestern Wildcats","result":"L","score":"42-14","values":[3,33,11,21,0,0,0,0,0,0]}]}},"summaryLabel":"2026 season stats","news":[{"headline":"Sources: Rutgers star KJ Duff out for season after ankle surgery","description":"KJ Duff, who projects as a first-round pick in the upcoming NFL draft, is expected to resume full football activities in January, sources said.","published":"2026-11-11T23:37:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50455958/rutgers-kj-duff-season-high-ankle-surgery-draft","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wyoming's Jay Sawvel gets self-imposed 1-game ban over tampering violations","description":"Wyoming coach Jay Sawvel will serve a one-game suspension Saturday as part of the school's self-imposed penalties for impermissible contacting of players.","published":"2026-11-25T00:01:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50586972/wyoming-coach-jay-sawvel-gets-self-imposed-1-game-suspension","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No. 20 Florida shuts down WR Vernell Brown for season-ending knee surgery","description":"No. 20 Florida is shutting down receiver Vernell Brown III for the remainder of the season.","published":"2026-11-24T23:07:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50586755/no-20-florida-shuts-wr-vernell-brown-season-ending-knee-surgery","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Viral couple from Wake Forest-Georgia Tech game speaks on 'Today' show","description":"The couple's intense discussion was caught on an ESPN broadcast of Wake Forest and Georgia Tech's Week 12 game and went viral.","published":"2026-11-24T21:02:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50584732/wake-forest-georgia-tech-viral-couple-speaks","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Colorado's Deion Sanders shrugs off hot-seat chatter before UCF","description":"Deion Sanders handles outside chatter -- in this case, speculation over his future as coach at Colorado -- by simply tuning out the noise.","published":"2026-11-24T21:29:37.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585728/colorado-sanders-shrugs-hot-seat-chatter-ucf","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Memphis' Charles Huff says he's not candidate for Maryland head coaching job","description":"Memphis' Charles Huff said he's not a candidate for the head coaching vacancy at Maryland and will not be part of this year's coaching carousel.","published":"2026-11-24T20:33:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585465/charles-huff-says-not-candidate-maryland-hc-job","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NCAA sanctions Liberty over tampering with two players before entering portal","description":"Among the penalties the NCAA announced against Liberty, two coaches and the GM received show-cause penalties over tampering.","published":"2026-11-24T20:05:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585093/ncaa-sanctions-liberty-transfer-portal-tampering","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Five-star OT Lincoln Fa'alafi commits to Notre Dame, to join 2028 class","description":"New Zealand native Lincoln Fa'alafi, ESPN's No. 8 overall prospect in the 2028 cycle, committed Tuesday to Notre Dame.","published":"2026-11-24T19:56:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50584881/notre-dame-gets-2028-commitment-ot-lincoln-faalafi","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"A timeline of Michigan athletics since 2017","description":"Warde Manuel's eventful decade in Ann Arbor has been marked by athletic successes and marred by controversy.","published":"2026-11-24T18:47:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49351177/2026-michigan-warde-manuel-athletic-department-tenure-line-investigation","type":"Story","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios in Week 13?","description":"Plenty of spots are still up for grabs entering the final week of the regular season.","published":"2026-11-24T18:22:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50583399/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-13","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5084771/kj-duff","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KJ_Duff"},"pick":{"pick":37,"round":2,"team":"ARI","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"KJ Duff","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KJ_Duff","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:18:07Z","intro":"Korey \"KJ\" Duff Jr. (born December 6, 2005) is an American college football wide receiver for the Rutgers Scarlet Knights.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Duff attended St. Anthony's High School  in South Huntington, New York. In his junior season, he hauled in 44 passes for 995 yards and 12 touchdowns. Coming out of high school, Duff was rated as a four-star recruit and committed to play college football for the Rutgers Scarlet Knights over schools such as Texas A&M, Miami, Pittsburgh, Arizona State, Duke, Georgia Tech, Maryland, Syracuse, Vanderbilt, and West Virginia."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Duff made his collegiate debut in the 2024 season opener against Howard, recording one reception for nine yards in a victory. The following week against Akron, he caught two passes for 29 yards and his first collegiate touchdown, a six-yard reception from Athan Kaliakmanis, in a 49–17 victory. In Week 8 against UCLA, Duff recorded a season-high 82 receiving yards on three receptions. In the Rate Bowl against Kansas State, he caught three passes for 58 yards in a 44–41 loss. He appeared in all 13 games with four starts, finishing the season with 27 receptions for 425 yards and one touchdown.\nDuff began the 2025 season with touchdown receptions in each of his first two games, victories over Ohio and Miami (OH). In Week 3 against Norfolk State, he recorded six receptions for 119 yards. In Week 8 against Purdue, Duff had six receptions for a career-high 241 yards and one touchdown in a 27–24 victory, with his receiving total ranking second in program history for a single game. Duff finished the season with 60 receptions for 1,084 yards and seven touchdowns, starting all 12 games, and was named second-team All-Big Ten.\nIn the 2026 season opener against UMass, Duff recorded nine receptions for 196 yards and three touchdowns in a loss. In Week 2 against Boston College, Duff recorded eight receptions for 137 yards and two touchdowns. He became the first Rutgers player to record at least 120 receiving yards in three consecutive games dating back to the 2025 season. He also recorded his 100th career reception in the loss."}]}}